From 8cf0bc49cb349c999db1c5ddcca54e0ec1f366be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam Day <me@samcday.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 16:25:28 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a3xx: flush HLSQ before indirect constant loads

On A306 (FD307), a draw whose constant update contains an indirect
(SS_INDIRECT) CP_LOAD_STATE of ST_CONSTANTS into the fragment state
block, following a direct upload to the same block and an earlier
indirect vertex-stage upload, hangs the GPU when another draw precedes
it in the same submit.  The CP ME stays busy on its register interface
while RBBM reports HLSQ, PC, VFD and VPC busy, until hangcheck
recovery.  GTK4's renderer hits this with its rounded-clip shaders, and
SuperTuxKart's benchmark can reset the SoC.

A CP_EVENT_WRITE HLSQ_FLUSH (or a CP_WAIT_FOR_IDLE) immediately before
the indirect load avoids it.  fd3_emit_state() already emits HLSQ_FLUSH
before all constant uploads, and adding one between the vertex and the
fragment uploads does not help either.  The kernel emits HLSQ_FLUSH at
the end of every submit so that nothing is pending for indirect loads,
which is why FD_MESA_DEBUG=flush hid the problem.

Emit HLSQ_FLUSH before every indirect constant load.  Flushing only
before fragment-stage loads fixes the reduced GTK4 trace but not
SuperTuxKart.  The loads stay indirect and rendering is unchanged
(bit-identical frames on the tested trace).

Tested on a DB410c (A306) with a Fedora 7.3-rc3 kernel carrying three
msm recovery/PM fixes and a Mesa 26.2.2 backport of this change: the
reduced GTK4 trace, the full trace in sysmem and GMEM mode, a GTK4
animation probe, GNOME Settings and supertuxkart --benchmark.

Closes: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/issues/12634

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a3xx/fd3_emit.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a3xx/fd3_emit.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a3xx/fd3_emit.c
index 69a5368..84b01e7 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a3xx/fd3_emit.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a3xx/fd3_emit.c
@@ -72,6 +72,15 @@ fd3_emit_const_bo(struct fd_ringbuffer *ring,
 
    emit_const_asserts(v, regid, sizedwords);
 
+   /* On a306, an indirect constant load that follows other constant loads
+    * in the same state update can hang unless HLSQ's lazy state updates are
+    * flushed first.  The kernel flushes them at the end of each submit for
+    * the same reason ("nothing pending for indirect loads"), so do it before
+    * every indirect load.
+    */
+   OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_EVENT_WRITE, 1);
+   OUT_RING(ring, HLSQ_FLUSH);
+
    OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_LOAD_STATE, 2);
    OUT_RING(ring, CP_LOAD_STATE_0_DST_OFF(dst_off) |
                      CP_LOAD_STATE_0_STATE_SRC(SS_INDIRECT) |
-- 
2.55.0

